00:14:23,140 --> 00:14:24,020
How much do you have left?

254
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:26,360
$5,200. Exactly.

255
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:30,040
What? I want it, okay?

256
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:32,920
Ben, we're gonna talk about this just as soon as I get rid of these kids.

257
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:34,020
Oh, don't worry, Dr.

258
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:37,840
Siever. We won't let any of those kids near Ben when we spend his next $5,000.

259
00:14:38,340 --> 00:14:42,300
If you boys actually think I'm gonna let Ben walk out that door with this much

260
00:14:42,300 --> 00:14:43,120
money, you're crazy.

261
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:44,260
You did before?

262
00:14:45,220 --> 00:14:47,120
Well, one of us did.

263
00:14:47,640 --> 00:14:49,480
Look, I'm not gonna spend a dime of this money.

264
00:14:49,740 --> 00:14:51,080
I don't even want this money.

265
00:14:51,180 --> 00:14:51,840
We'll take it!

266
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:52,480
We'll take it!

267
00:14:52,720 --> 00:14:53,440
Hey, hey, hey!

268
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:54,440
Cut your own half, Doctor.

269
00:14:54,440 --> 00:14:55,420
Yeah, who needs Ben?

270
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:58,560
Hey, if all you care about is my money, then get out!

271
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:02,020
If we stay, what do we get?

272
00:15:02,720 --> 00:15:03,620
Out, out, out!

273
00:15:04,660 --> 00:15:08,780
I bought you guys CDs, I bought you guys the jackets, I even bought you guys

274
00:15:08,780 --> 00:15:11,540
underwear! You bought stinky underwear?

275
00:15:12,060 --> 00:15:13,520
No, it was new.

276
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:21,020
Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah.

277
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:26,300
Not many buyers are shrewd enough to test -drive a car with the top off in the dead

278
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:29,080
of winter. This thing does have a top, though, right?

279
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:30,020
Of course it does.

280
00:15:30,040 --> 00:15:31,960
What kind of a businessman do you think I am?

281
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:33,780
It's on order.

282
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:36,960
Boy, I love this thing.

283
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:39,860
Like I said, 5,700, out the door.

284
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:41,720
Wait a minute, you said 4,700.

285
00:15:41,900 --> 00:15:43,800
Deal. Let's sign the paper.

286
00:15:50,420 --> 00:16:01,540
Mike? It sure is cold out here.

287
00:16:01,760 --> 00:16:02,960
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

288
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:06,520
Uh, so, will you be giving me the whole 5,700 in cash?

289
00:16:08,260 --> 00:16:10,760
Ben, I think maybe you're being a little bit extreme.

290
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:14,180
All I said was that I hope Sneaky and Jerry explode.

291
00:16:14,580 --> 00:16:16,040
What's extreme about that?

292
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:19,760
Hello, everybody. Carol.

293
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:21,560
We really don't have time for that.

294
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:22,960
Where's Claire and my grandpa?

295
00:16:23,180 --> 00:16:24,360
Hopefully they exploded.

296
00:16:25,140 --> 00:16:26,460
They're in the kitchen, honey.

297
00:16:28,220 --> 00:16:31,600
You are so helpful on the inconsequential questions.

298
00:16:33,160 --> 00:16:35,380
Dad, cut the baloney and get down here.

299
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:41,040
Now! Eddie, you don't suppose our gifts to the kids have caused tension around here,

300
00:16:41,040 --> 00:16:44,720
do you? Oh, good, you're both here.

301
00:16:45,740 --> 00:16:50,060
Well, I was out walking for two hours I was trying to figure out the best way to

302
00:16:50,060 --> 00:16:50,800
spend this money.

303
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:55,320
I wanted something that could begin to repay you for knitting, Mr.

304
00:16:55,340 --> 00:16:57,480
Blanky. I didn't knit that.

305
00:16:57,540 --> 00:16:58,600
I found it.

306
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:02,860
You what? I think we're getting off the track here.

307
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:04,120
Why don't you let the child talk?

308
00:17:04,700 --> 00:17:07,700
Well, you said I could spend it any way that would make me happy.

309
00:17:08,100 --> 00:17:09,880
So, this is what I bought.

310
00:17:10,620 --> 00:17:12,720
Oh. What the heck is this, now?

311
00:17:13,300 --> 00:17:15,940
Two first -class round -trip tickets to Ireland.

312
00:17:15,940 --> 00:17:19,760
Carol, I had no idea you wanted to go to Ireland.

313
00:17:20,860 --> 00:17:22,660
Not for me, for you two.

314
00:17:23,840 --> 00:17:27,200
For us. Oh, that's wonderful.

315
00:17:27,860 --> 00:17:31,320
Look, if I had wanted to take a trip to Ireland, I could have bought it myself.

316
00:17:31,700 --> 00:17:33,680
Well, sure, you could have, but you didn't.

317
00:17:33,940 --> 00:17:35,420
You gave the money to us instead.

318
00:17:35,900 --> 00:17:39,140
Exactly. That's why you had no business doing this.

319
00:17:39,820 --> 00:17:43,420
Well, you said you wanted the pleasure of watching us spend it, so here.

320
00:17:43,420 --> 00:17:47,020
I had the travel agent take it as I gave him the money.

321
00:17:48,020 --> 00:17:54,100
Oh. Honey, I -I don't know what to say.

322
00:17:54,780 --> 00:18:00,480
Oh. I just want you two to be careful in Ireland because they drive on the other

323
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:01,420
side of the road there.

324
00:18:01,740 --> 00:18:06,200
Oh, Eddie, all these years, you've been driving in the wrong country.

325
00:18:08,980 --> 00:18:11,820
I don't understand is how money turns people into pigs.

326
00:18:11,820 --> 00:18:14,880
Well, Ben, that's a start just to realize the money did change you.

327
00:18:15,080 --> 00:18:16,720
Not me, Stinky and Gary.

328
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:20,840
Ben, tell me, just how did they force you to buy all these things?

329
00:18:21,420 --> 00:18:22,400
Uh, force me?

330
00:18:22,820 --> 00:18:24,600
Well, they were very tricky about it.

331
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:27,720
Probably made it seem like it was your idea, right?

332
00:18:28,140 --> 00:18:30,120
Yeah. Well, there's a reason for that, Ben.

333
00:18:30,460 --> 00:18:31,540
It was your idea.

334
00:18:33,340 --> 00:18:36,340
So you think I blew $5,000 on purpose?

335
00:18:36,660 --> 00:18:38,840
No, I think you probably just lost your head.

336
00:18:38,840 --> 00:18:42,700
Me? Didn't you see Stinky and Gary tug it on that chuck like animals?

337
00:18:42,900 --> 00:18:44,720
Oh, kind of like you and Mike did this morning?

338
00:18:44,940 --> 00:18:48,420
Yeah. Oh. Ah.

339
00:18:48,980 --> 00:18:50,860
You just had an important thought there, Ben.

340
00:18:51,120 --> 00:18:52,400
I was afraid of that.

341
00:18:53,940 --> 00:18:57,380
So not only did I blow $5,000, I was wrong, too.

342
00:18:57,680 --> 00:18:58,960
That about sums it up.

343
00:18:59,500 --> 00:19:03,640
So, Ben, what are we going to do with all your winnings?

344
00:19:04,240 --> 00:19:07,140
Well, you could give me another shot to spend it any way I want.

345
00:19:07,140 --> 00:19:09,480
Is that really what you think?

346
00:19:09,580 --> 00:19:11,980
No, I just figured we all needed a good laugh about now.

347
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:19,180
Maggie, Jason, our granddaughter just did the most wonderful thing with her money.

348
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:23,140
That figures. Ben, you're in pain.

349
00:19:23,380 --> 00:19:27,240
How sad. She's sending us out of the country.

350
00:19:28,060 --> 00:19:30,200
Carol, that is a terrific idea.

351
00:19:31,320 --> 00:19:32,560
You're so predictable.

352
00:19:33,480 --> 00:19:35,460
Ben, come on, tell me from your sister.

353
00:19:35,460 --> 00:19:36,780
What? How to eat?

354
00:19:39,420 --> 00:19:43,220
What's that? You didn't buy a car, too, did you?

355
00:19:43,680 --> 00:19:51,600
I might've. Ta -da!

356
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:52,700
All right, all right.

357
00:19:52,700 --> 00:19:53,260
What do you think?

358
00:19:53,340 --> 00:19:54,140
Come on, be honest.

359
00:19:55,120 --> 00:19:57,760
Well, at least you didn't blow all your money at once.

360
00:19:58,120 --> 00:19:59,300
What do you mean, blow my money?

361
00:19:59,460 --> 00:20:00,940
Dad, this is a great car.

362
00:20:01,380 --> 00:20:02,780
He spent every dime.

363
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:05,560
Just to wait the dad blame minute.

364
00:20:05,860 --> 00:20:08,260
Mike, are you happy with the way you spent your money?

365
00:20:08,620 --> 00:20:11,480
Oh, Grandpa, I've never been happier about anything in my whole life.

366
00:20:11,800 --> 00:20:13,280
Well, then, case closed.

367
00:20:14,780 --> 00:20:16,100
I don't get it.

368
00:20:16,380 --> 00:20:17,480
What did he buy?

369
00:20:17,820 --> 00:20:19,320
A piece of junk in the driveway.

370
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:25,600
Hey, I'm telling you, once I fix this baby up, you won't even recognize her.

371
00:20:25,720 --> 00:20:27,820
But you have no money left to fix it up with.

372
00:20:27,980 --> 00:20:29,820
Ah, details, details.

373
00:20:30,720 --> 00:20:32,720
Look, I'm gonna go show this off to my friends.

374
00:20:32,720 --> 00:20:33,840
I'll see you later.

375
00:20:38,520 --> 00:20:41,500
Well, Jason, for what it's worth, I don't blame you for this.

376
00:20:42,120 --> 00:20:42,640
Of course not.

377
00:20:42,680 --> 00:20:43,520
We raised them.

378
00:20:43,660 --> 00:20:45,740
Oh. Well, look on the bright side.

379
00:20:46,040 --> 00:20:50,080
Carol did something nice, and Ben learned something in spite of himself, and...

380
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:52,920
And Mike continued his perfect record of irresponsibility.

381
00:20:53,340 --> 00:20:55,960
Well, it is a perfect record.

382
00:20:57,360 --> 00:21:01,840
Oh, there. Uh, excuse me.

383
00:21:01,840 --> 00:21:04,140
Um, Michael at home?

384
00:21:04,760 --> 00:21:06,980
Uh, uh, you just missed him.

385
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:13,560
Oh, drat. Well, would you give him these for his new vehicle?

386
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:17,880
And, oh, he forgot my IOU.

387
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:24,040
$3,500? Mike gave you...

388
00:21:24,040 --> 00:21:25,620
He didn't give me nothing.

389
00:21:26,340 --> 00:21:33,300
I consider it merely as a short -term loan, which I will repay in full as soon as I

390
00:21:33,300 --> 00:21:34,680
return from Florida.

391
00:21:35,700 --> 00:21:37,320
What do you know?

392
00:21:37,840 --> 00:21:40,920
I hear they got a lot of women there with teeth.

393
00:21:42,360 --> 00:21:47,160
Teeth? Yeah. Maybe I'll even find a little snouser for Lloyd.

394
00:21:53,980 --> 00:21:57,280
Well, there goes his perfect record.

395
00:21:57,920 --> 00:21:59,780
I never doubted the boy for a minute.

396
00:21:59,780 --> 00:22:05,200
Ha! Nice, huh?

397
00:22:05,780 --> 00:22:07,980
We'll be back in a moment.

398
00:22:12,360 --> 00:22:13,240
I got a promotion!

399
00:22:13,520 --> 00:22:18,300
I'm the manager of the punctuation department with my own office, people reporting

400
00:22:18,300 --> 00:22:19,280
to me, and everything.

401
00:22:19,660 --> 00:22:21,620
Carol, it's for you, some guy.

402
00:22:22,020 --> 00:22:23,940
You expect me to fall for that?

403
00:22:24,680 --> 00:22:26,400
I'm sorry, she doesn't know any guys.

404
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:30,780
Well, she can't come to the phone right now.

405
00:22:31,520 --> 00:22:33,680
If you must know, she's in the can.

406
00:22:36,800 --> 00:22:38,420
Is there really somebody on the phone?

407
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:39,460
Yeah, oh, yeah.

408
00:22:39,460 --> 00:22:40,840
He says he's from your work.

409
00:22:40,860 --> 00:22:42,080
He says it's an emergency.

410
00:22:42,460 --> 00:22:43,500
Well, that's impossible.

411
00:22:44,360 --> 00:22:46,900
You expect her to climb off the throne for that?
